---
title: BUTTON - momentary push button
---
%% Driver takes any port/pin; no defaults in code.
%% PA0 is the on-board B1 (active HIGH on this board).
%% PE2 is free in project.ioc and shown as the conventional active-low button.
%% No external resistor needed - enable the internal pull-up or pull-down.
flowchart LR
    subgraph MCU["STM32F429I-DISC1"]
        PA0["PA0 - on-board B1"]
        PE2["PE2 - external button"]
        V33["3V3"]
        GND["GND"]
    end

    B1["On-board B1 - pulls PA0 high when pressed"]
    BX["External button - active low"]
    PU["Internal pull-up enabled in software"]

    V33 --- B1
    PA0 ---|"pressed = high"| B1
    PE2 -.-|"internal pull-up"| PU
    PE2 --- BX
    GND --- BX
